1
00:00:05,033 --> 00:00:11,900
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,967 --> 00:00:33,433
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,433 --> 00:00:35,533
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,533 --> 00:00:41,533
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,833 --> 00:00:44,333
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,333 --> 00:00:45,533
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,533 --> 00:00:47,067
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:47,067 --> 00:00:48,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:51,767
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,933 --> 00:00:54,100
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:55,833
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,900 --> 00:00:58,500
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:59,333 --> 00:01:00,567
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:03,567
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,433 --> 00:01:06,533
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:09,300
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,333 --> 00:01:11,700
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:13,367
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,367 --> 00:01:15,233
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,833 --> 00:01:23,900
<i>And now they know we're not
to be messed with.</i>

21
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:25,367
<i>We can't just do nothing
about what happened.</i>

22
00:01:25,367 --> 00:01:26,433
<i> We need to strike back.</i>

23
00:01:26,433 --> 00:01:29,067
<i>How did they find out
about our tribute dinner?</i>

24
00:01:29,067 --> 00:01:32,033
<i> I almost died!</i>

25
00:01:32,033 --> 00:01:34,600
<i>We're paying you to betray
your colleagues.</i>

26
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:35,733
- [LOUD SLAP]
- [GASPS]  Ma!

27
00:01:35,733 --> 00:01:37,100
<i> And don't forget.</i>

28
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:41,300
<i>I'm your last resort
to get your son out!</i>

29
00:01:41,333 --> 00:01:44,100
<i> Gloria, look! They all came!</i>

30
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:46,400
<i>It's amusing that you guys
took me seriously.</i>

31
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:48,767
<i>- Nice fit, Gabo!
- Wow!</i>

32
00:01:48,767 --> 00:01:49,733
<i> I'll go look for a job.</i>

33
00:01:49,833 --> 00:01:51,467
<i>Are you not going to give her
a goodbye kiss?</i>

34
00:01:51,467 --> 00:01:53,133
<i> Oh, hell no! Absolutely not!</i>

35
00:01:53,133 --> 00:01:55,133
<i>- Right here.
- Just on the cheek.</i>

36
00:01:55,967 --> 00:01:59,500
[CHEERING, APPLAUSE]

37
00:02:01,233 --> 00:02:02,700
[TWINKLE] Ma'am Isobel,

38
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:04,867
would you like
to have some breakfast?

39
00:02:09,033 --> 00:02:10,967
Thank you, but I'm not hungry.

40
00:02:11,233 --> 00:02:12,433
I feel the same, ma'am.

41
00:02:12,667 --> 00:02:14,300
I don't have an appetite either.

42
00:02:18,933 --> 00:02:20,033
[ISOBEL] Why?

43
00:02:20,667 --> 00:02:22,033
Is there something
troubling you?

44
00:02:22,667 --> 00:02:24,500
It's Toto.

45
00:02:24,833 --> 00:02:26,967
He was crying all night.

46
00:02:27,367 --> 00:02:28,600
I did too.

47
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:29,933
[CHAIR CLATTERS LIGHTLY]

48
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:32,367
It's like I'll never
run out of tears.

49
00:02:32,667 --> 00:02:33,833
For Sam.

50
00:02:34,667 --> 00:02:39,100
Toto wasn't crying
because of Ma'am Sam's loss.

51
00:02:39,633 --> 00:02:41,300
[SIGHS HEAVILY]

52
00:02:42,533 --> 00:02:44,267
It was because of Madam Rosa.

53
00:02:44,267 --> 00:02:46,733
- Huh?
- She's got such a sharp tongue!

54
00:02:46,733 --> 00:02:48,767
Toto just had his future read.

55
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:51,567
Not only was she snarky at him
she insulted him too!

56
00:02:51,567 --> 00:02:53,200
Did she have to be like that?

57
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:55,967
Couldn't she have predicted
that she'll hurt his feelings?

58
00:02:55,967 --> 00:02:59,233
Also, is Madam Rosa
actually legit?

59
00:02:59,633 --> 00:03:00,800
She's probably not.

60
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:04,567
Maybe she was tired. You just
caught her at a bad time.

61
00:03:04,567 --> 00:03:07,067
Maybe she read too many people
that day

62
00:03:07,067 --> 00:03:08,733
and talked to many clients.

63
00:03:08,733 --> 00:03:10,533
Just tell Toto that...

64
00:03:11,467 --> 00:03:13,633
he shouldn't take it to heart.

65
00:03:14,567 --> 00:03:15,767
Alright, ma'am.

66
00:03:17,967 --> 00:03:19,067
[TWINKLE] Thank you.

67
00:03:19,067 --> 00:03:25,600
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

68
00:03:25,633 --> 00:03:26,700
[CLEARS THROAT]

69
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:30,767
First of all, thank you
to everyone who already started.

70
00:03:30,767 --> 00:03:33,233
But before anything else,
let's establish a system first

71
00:03:33,233 --> 00:03:35,933
to make our work more effective
and efficient.

72
00:03:36,267 --> 00:03:39,100
First, the sweepers. Who wants
to sweep the streets?

73
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:40,167
Let's elect some people.

74
00:03:40,167 --> 00:03:42,000
Me, Gloria! I'd like to be
on the sweepers team!

75
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,067
- Us too!
- Us!

76
00:03:43,067 --> 00:03:45,667
- We're good at it!
- Let us join, Gloria!

77
00:03:45,667 --> 00:03:48,167
Okay, you guys will be
the sweepers team.

78
00:03:48,167 --> 00:03:50,033
- Alright!
- This is fun.

79
00:03:50,033 --> 00:03:52,500
Ipe, Binoy, and Daboy,

80
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:55,467
you guys will be in charge
of the biodegradable wastes.

81
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:56,733
- The biodegradable team.
- Okay.

82
00:03:56,733 --> 00:03:59,733
Gather all biodegradable wastes
together

83
00:03:59,733 --> 00:04:01,067
because we could use them
as compost.

84
00:04:01,067 --> 00:04:03,733
We can use them as fertilizer
for the plants we'll plant here.

85
00:04:03,733 --> 00:04:05,833
Do your best. We'll be
the rotten team.

86
00:04:05,833 --> 00:04:07,367
What rotten? It's biodegradable!

87
00:04:07,367 --> 00:04:09,400
- Biodegradable!
- This team fits you, huh.

88
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,433
Alright. Tolits, Bong, and Tekla

89
00:04:12,433 --> 00:04:14,567
you will be in charge
of the non-biodegradable.

90
00:04:14,567 --> 00:04:17,633
Bottles, papers, things we can
sell at the junk shop

91
00:04:17,633 --> 00:04:19,200
and turn into handicrafts.
I'll leave it to you.

92
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:20,600
Oh, I refuse. Sorry.

93
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:23,867
I just had my nails done.
They might break.

94
00:04:23,867 --> 00:04:26,033
I'll supervise everyone instead

95
00:04:26,033 --> 00:04:27,500
so I'll tell everyone
what they should do.

96
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:30,800
I'll go around, controlling
and telling everyone what to do.

97
00:04:30,833 --> 00:04:33,467
- Listen to me properly, okay?
- [CLEARS THROAT] Uh...

98
00:04:33,467 --> 00:04:37,633
We're good with that.
We're the uh, recycling team.

99
00:04:37,633 --> 00:04:39,367
- Recycling team!
- Just you guys.

100
00:04:39,367 --> 00:04:41,567
I don't look like it
but I'm useful!

101
00:04:41,567 --> 00:04:43,867
We'll serve you even if
we don't look too useful.

102
00:04:43,867 --> 00:04:47,333
[ALL EXCLAIMING, LAUGHING,
APPLAUDING]

103
00:04:47,333 --> 00:04:48,567
Thanks for that.

104
00:04:48,567 --> 00:04:49,800
Alright,

105
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:51,433
-we now have our recycling team.
- [TEKLA] Leave me out of it!

106
00:04:51,433 --> 00:04:53,600
Who here can withstand
strong smells?

107
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,533
They can clean up our sewers.

108
00:04:55,533 --> 00:04:57,033
We'll take care of it, buddy!

109
00:04:57,033 --> 00:04:59,367
I'm immune to the smell
of my husband's armpits!

110
00:04:59,367 --> 00:05:02,033
[LAUGHTER]

111
00:05:02,067 --> 00:05:04,167
No wonder you cling to me
every night!

112
00:05:04,167 --> 00:05:07,733
[EXCLAIMING, APPLAUDING]

113
00:05:07,733 --> 00:05:10,033
But wait, everyone.
Not all of us has to leave.

114
00:05:10,033 --> 00:05:12,533
Some of us have to be left here
at our sorting area.

115
00:05:12,533 --> 00:05:14,367
The waste that each group
will pick up

116
00:05:14,367 --> 00:05:15,767
will be dumped here.

117
00:05:15,767 --> 00:05:17,900
- Got it!
- But wait a sec.

118
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:19,733
What can I do to help?

119
00:05:19,733 --> 00:05:21,833
Auntie, can I entrust you
to kitchen duties?

120
00:05:21,833 --> 00:05:23,267
So we can have snacks
to eat later.

121
00:05:23,267 --> 00:05:25,667
[CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

122
00:05:25,667 --> 00:05:27,367
Macaroni soup!
We love macaroni soup!

123
00:05:27,367 --> 00:05:29,467
That's the most delicious idea
I've ever heard!

124
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:32,167
That's perfect
because I'm already used

125
00:05:32,167 --> 00:05:34,667
to feeding these guys
every day at home.

126
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:36,200
- Look at him.
- Yeah!

127
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:37,967
I'm proud of you, babe.

128
00:05:37,967 --> 00:05:39,833
[ALL EXCLAIMING, APPLAUDING]

129
00:05:39,833 --> 00:05:41,267
Don't worry, Ms. Mameng.

130
00:05:41,267 --> 00:05:44,700
I'll be your tester.
I'll take on that job instead!

131
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:47,733
No need. You'll just make things
complicated for me.

132
00:05:47,733 --> 00:05:49,100
[TEKLA] Oh, come on!

133
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:51,600
[SAM] Hold on, we still have
roles to fill, um...

134
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:52,933
Does anyone here know
how to paint?

135
00:05:52,933 --> 00:05:54,867
- We need one for the signages.
- [MAMENG] Oh!

136
00:05:54,867 --> 00:05:57,000
- Me! I'll do it!
- Who's that?

137
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,367
I used to be a makeup artist.

138
00:05:58,367 --> 00:06:00,500
No, no, I'll do it.

139
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:02,533
Be my assistant instead.
I'll do the painting.

140
00:06:02,533 --> 00:06:04,433
- Deal!
- Alright, we have a deal.

141
00:06:04,433 --> 00:06:05,533
I have a job now, okay?

142
00:06:05,533 --> 00:06:07,300
- Hey, Tekla!
- That's fine!

143
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:09,700
You shouldered everything!

144
00:06:09,733 --> 00:06:12,167
Why do you care?! I have
freedom of speech here, right?

145
00:06:12,167 --> 00:06:14,200
You're saying I can't pick
a job I want?

146
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:16,067
Uh, Tekla, I'm sorry.

147
00:06:16,067 --> 00:06:17,867
If I give in to you,

148
00:06:17,867 --> 00:06:20,133
of course, I'd have to give in
to the others too.

149
00:06:20,133 --> 00:06:21,800
Things might get a bit messy.

150
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:24,033
[TEKLA LAUGHS]

151
00:06:24,033 --> 00:06:25,333
Why are you joining
in our conversation?

152
00:06:25,333 --> 00:06:26,933
We're the ones talking, right?

153
00:06:26,933 --> 00:06:28,067
- Shush.
- You know what?

154
00:06:28,067 --> 00:06:30,300
I'm out. I'm out!
You can clean it yourselves.

155
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:32,200
I've lost interest!

156
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:33,933
Do it by yourself.
Since you're a show-off!

157
00:06:33,933 --> 00:06:35,300
- I'm off.
- Hey, Tekla!

158
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:37,400
You've changed a lot!

159
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:38,467
Tekla!

160
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:39,967
Friends,

161
00:06:39,967 --> 00:06:42,133
let her be for now.
Let's form a group.

162
00:06:42,167 --> 00:06:44,567
Let's talk about what group
you'll be joining in.

163
00:06:44,567 --> 00:06:46,000
Is that okay? Let's start!

164
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:51,867
[PEOPLE CLAPPING, CHEERING]

165
00:06:51,867 --> 00:06:52,900
[TWINKLE] Ma'am.

166
00:06:53,900 --> 00:06:55,233
She's here again.

167
00:06:55,233 --> 00:06:58,033
Thank you, Twinkle. Thank you.

168
00:06:58,033 --> 00:06:59,867
- [ISOBEL] Madam Rosa, come!
- Oh!

169
00:06:59,867 --> 00:07:02,967
- The food is ready.
- Isob-- wow!

170
00:07:02,967 --> 00:07:05,100
It's my favorite!

171
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:06,700
Thank you!

172
00:07:06,700 --> 00:07:09,000
Thank you!

173
00:07:10,367 --> 00:07:11,867
Madam Rosa.

174
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:13,900
What's the news?

175
00:07:15,167 --> 00:07:17,533
Did Sam make her
presence felt again?

176
00:07:17,533 --> 00:07:19,233
Did she say anything?

177
00:07:20,167 --> 00:07:21,833
Ah...

178
00:07:21,833 --> 00:07:24,000
Madam Rosa,
I have a question for you.

179
00:07:24,333 --> 00:07:26,600
It is Sam I'm talking to, right?

180
00:07:27,533 --> 00:07:29,667
And she is the one
possessing you?

181
00:07:30,233 --> 00:07:33,467
Isobel, listen to
what your heart is saying.

182
00:07:36,633 --> 00:07:38,100
Ah...

183
00:07:38,100 --> 00:07:40,567
Don't you have a lot of...

184
00:07:40,567 --> 00:07:42,700
Spirits that you
have put to rest?

185
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:46,233
And your predictions
came true, right?

186
00:07:47,333 --> 00:07:48,467
Isobel...

187
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:53,633
You won't know Madam Rosa
if she is a fraud.

188
00:07:55,167 --> 00:07:58,433
Where are these doubts
coming from?

189
00:07:58,433 --> 00:08:02,200
[WHIMSICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

190
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:04,033
[INHALES SHARPLY] Ah! Nothing!

191
00:08:04,033 --> 00:08:06,233
Nothing! I am not doubting you.

192
00:08:06,233 --> 00:08:07,267
No.

193
00:08:08,367 --> 00:08:09,700
Isobel.

194
00:08:10,167 --> 00:08:12,667
Madam Rosa is huge.

195
00:08:12,667 --> 00:08:14,533
- Huge?
- Has a huge radar.

196
00:08:14,533 --> 00:08:17,233
Luzon, Visayas, Mindanao.

197
00:08:17,300 --> 00:08:20,133
Even in Asia
and the whole of Earth.

198
00:08:20,133 --> 00:08:22,100
She knows
what's going to happen.

199
00:08:23,233 --> 00:08:25,767
It's important for you to hear
about Samantha,

200
00:08:25,767 --> 00:08:27,233
- isn't it?
- Yes!

201
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:29,767
I'd like to know...

202
00:08:29,767 --> 00:08:31,533
if she's making
her presence felt.

203
00:08:31,533 --> 00:08:33,900
I didn't sleep all night.

204
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:35,233
[BREATH SHAKING] Why?

205
00:08:35,233 --> 00:08:38,200
What's her message?
Isn't she in peace?

206
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:41,100
It was not Sam's voice
I'm hearing.

207
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:46,167
It was the voices of the spirits
disturbing her!

208
00:08:46,633 --> 00:08:51,533
Do you want to know why I
wasn't able to sleep last night?

209
00:08:51,533 --> 00:08:55,833
You said it was because of
those restless souls!

210
00:08:55,933 --> 00:08:56,967
No!

211
00:08:58,100 --> 00:08:59,967
Because our electricity was cut.

212
00:08:59,967 --> 00:09:02,433
It's hard to sleep
when it's hot!

213
00:09:02,433 --> 00:09:06,833
That's why I wasn't able
to talk to Samantha.

214
00:09:06,833 --> 00:09:09,300
I was so sleep-deprived
last night!

215
00:09:10,667 --> 00:09:12,867
Look at my eyes.

216
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:16,367
Oh! You're under eyes
are indeed dark!

217
00:09:16,967 --> 00:09:22,433
I don't know when I'll be able
to sleep peacefully again!

218
00:09:22,433 --> 00:09:25,867
I don't know when
Madam Rosa will be able to talk

219
00:09:25,867 --> 00:09:27,800
to your daughter, Samantha.

220
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:30,500
Madam Rosa also has children.

221
00:09:30,533 --> 00:09:34,633
She has three children
to care for!

222
00:09:34,633 --> 00:09:38,200
But Madam Rosa is struggling!

223
00:09:39,533 --> 00:09:41,467
Madam Rosa's good heart

224
00:09:41,533 --> 00:09:44,500
just wants to help her neighbor.

225
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:46,733
[CRYING] But who's
going to help--

226
00:09:47,167 --> 00:09:49,667
- her?
- Me!

227
00:09:49,667 --> 00:09:51,733
[CRYING] I'll help you!

228
00:09:51,733 --> 00:09:54,267
I'm ready to help you!

229
00:09:54,267 --> 00:09:55,700
Wait a minute.

230
00:09:55,767 --> 00:09:57,467
Twinkle, come with me.

231
00:09:57,467 --> 00:09:59,567
- Ma'am?
- Come with me upstairs.

232
00:10:00,333 --> 00:10:02,333
- Just eat there.
- Yes!

233
00:10:02,367 --> 00:10:04,200
[CRYING]

234
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:07,167
[LAUGHING]

235
00:10:07,167 --> 00:10:08,200
Ah!

236
00:10:08,667 --> 00:10:10,233
Just eat there.

237
00:10:11,833 --> 00:10:13,667
Hmm. Delicious.

238
00:10:14,100 --> 00:10:16,267
- Gabo! Looking good!
- Of course!

239
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:23,100
Miss, can I do a cash-in here?

240
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:25,000
- How much?
- 500 pesos.

241
00:10:28,267 --> 00:10:35,033
- Number?
- 09913035077.

242
00:10:35,067 --> 00:10:36,433
- Name?
- Eric.

243
00:10:37,667 --> 00:10:39,600
Hey, Gabo! Where are you off to?

244
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:40,867
I'm going job hunting!

245
00:10:40,867 --> 00:10:42,033
You have a nice get-up!

246
00:10:42,033 --> 00:10:44,467
Of course, my wife
takes good care of me.

247
00:10:44,467 --> 00:10:46,233
Right! You have a wife now!

248
00:10:46,233 --> 00:10:47,667
What's her name?

249
00:10:47,667 --> 00:10:48,867
Gloria.

250
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:50,833
[VENDOR] There's no
account registered!

251
00:10:50,833 --> 00:10:52,267
Let me see.

252
00:10:52,267 --> 00:10:53,467
- Here.
- Let me.

253
00:10:56,733 --> 00:10:58,333
Here. It's done.

254
00:10:59,967 --> 00:11:00,967
Oh, okay.

255
00:11:00,967 --> 00:11:02,433
- Thanks, miss.
- Okay.

256
00:11:02,433 --> 00:11:04,633
Oh! That was 5,000!

257
00:11:04,633 --> 00:11:06,400
Hey! Scammer!

258
00:11:06,400 --> 00:11:07,967
Hey! He's a scammer!

259
00:11:09,733 --> 00:11:10,867
Scammer!

260
00:11:11,433 --> 00:11:12,700
Hey!

261
00:11:12,700 --> 00:11:13,733
Scammer!

262
00:11:13,733 --> 00:11:14,767
Move out of the way!
He's a scammer!

263
00:11:14,767 --> 00:11:15,833
[BLOW LANDING]

264
00:11:17,033 --> 00:11:18,900
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [MEN GRUNTING]

265
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:23,100
- [PEOPLE SCREAMING]
- [OBJECTS FALLING]

266
00:11:24,533 --> 00:11:26,200
[GABO] You're sick in the head!

267
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:27,667
You're trying to scam
people here?!

268
00:11:28,833 --> 00:11:31,700
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [MEN GRUNTING]

269
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:34,733
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

270
00:11:36,567 --> 00:11:39,067
[BLOWS LANDING]

271
00:11:39,067 --> 00:11:42,633
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

272
00:11:42,667 --> 00:11:44,133
[BLOWS LANDING]

273
00:11:47,033 --> 00:11:48,200
Get him up!

274
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:50,400
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- Get him before he gets away!

275
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:54,767
[BLOWS LANDING]

276
00:11:58,867 --> 00:11:59,933
He's a criminal!

277
00:11:59,933 --> 00:12:04,900
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

278
00:12:04,900 --> 00:12:06,233
You're out of your mind!

279
00:12:06,233 --> 00:12:08,367
Of all the places
you can mess with,

280
00:12:08,367 --> 00:12:10,000
you went here to
Ginintuang Lupa!

281
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:15,467
Go! Bring him to the station!

282
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:17,867
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

283
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:21,400
- Hey!
- Come on!

284
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:23,633
- Hey!
- I said no!

285
00:12:23,633 --> 00:12:25,167
Leave me alone!

286
00:12:25,167 --> 00:12:26,833
Come on, Tekla.

287
00:12:26,833 --> 00:12:28,433
Don't let your
emotions get in the way.

288
00:12:28,433 --> 00:12:29,667
Oh, shut up!
Let me go!

289
00:12:29,667 --> 00:12:32,800
- Don't touch me!
- We're not touching you!

290
00:12:33,467 --> 00:12:37,967
Tekla, could you please
just do this for Gabo?

291
00:12:37,967 --> 00:12:39,133
Now wait a minute.

292
00:12:39,133 --> 00:12:41,400
What does Gabo
have to do with this?

293
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:43,467
He wants us all to help,
remember?

294
00:12:43,467 --> 00:12:46,067
Why the hell should I
follow that girl's orders?

295
00:12:46,067 --> 00:12:47,367
It was her idea.

296
00:12:47,367 --> 00:12:49,200
Then she should do it.

297
00:12:49,233 --> 00:12:51,133
Tekla, what do you think
Gabo will say

298
00:12:51,133 --> 00:12:52,500
if he finds out you didn't help?

299
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:53,833
[IPE] Be reasonable, Tekla.

300
00:12:53,833 --> 00:12:56,200
It's just a one-time thing.

301
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:57,267
Just do it.

302
00:12:57,267 --> 00:12:58,267
Come on!

303
00:12:58,267 --> 00:13:00,433
How about this, Tekla?

304
00:13:00,433 --> 00:13:04,200
If you go home,
it means you love me.

305
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:06,700
- Hmm?
- But if you don't,

306
00:13:06,700 --> 00:13:08,267
that means you love Gabo.

307
00:13:08,267 --> 00:13:09,467
So I guess you should go home!

308
00:13:09,467 --> 00:13:12,067
Oh, what a bright idea.

309
00:13:12,067 --> 00:13:14,700
But I'll just help you guys out.
Come on, let's go!

310
00:13:14,700 --> 00:13:16,433
- Good call.
- Whatever.

311
00:13:16,433 --> 00:13:18,167
- Tell Daboy to get lost.
- Get lost, dude.

312
00:13:18,167 --> 00:13:19,433
Go home.

313
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,600
- Hand me the plastic bottles.
- Come on!

314
00:13:23,633 --> 00:13:24,600
This won't take long!

315
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:26,900
I thought we were here
to clean up?

316
00:13:26,900 --> 00:13:29,000
- We'll be quick. Gloria!
- Why is Daboy here?

317
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,433
Gloria! We did it.
She agreed to help!

318
00:13:31,433 --> 00:13:32,900
You're going to help us,
aren't you?

319
00:13:32,900 --> 00:13:34,700
- Fine!
- I've convinced her.

320
00:13:34,700 --> 00:13:37,233
But I'll decide
what I want to do.

321
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:38,867
You can't boss me around.

322
00:13:38,867 --> 00:13:40,067
All right, come on.

323
00:13:40,067 --> 00:13:41,633
- Let's get started.
- Dig in.

324
00:13:41,633 --> 00:13:43,967
- Come on!
- I'll follow your lead.

325
00:13:43,967 --> 00:13:46,133
- What's this?
- Oh.

326
00:13:46,133 --> 00:13:49,333
This can be recycled, right?

327
00:13:49,333 --> 00:13:52,033
We can turn it
into a Molotov cocktail.

328
00:13:52,033 --> 00:13:54,933
This just needs to be sharpened,
and it can be used as a weapon.

329
00:13:54,967 --> 00:13:57,733
Look, it can be used
to smash someone's head.

330
00:13:57,733 --> 00:14:00,200
- [BINOY SCATTING]
- [GLORIA] Guys, that's enough.

331
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:02,800
We're cleaning up,
not trying to start a riot.

332
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:04,533
Can't you take a joke?

333
00:14:04,533 --> 00:14:06,200
That's how we work here.
We joke around.

334
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:07,533
Or is that not allowed too?

335
00:14:07,533 --> 00:14:10,300
Sorry, it's just that
you guys always start trouble

336
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:12,433
so I can't tell whether
you're joking or not.

337
00:14:13,133 --> 00:14:14,933
Well, I wonder why...

338
00:14:14,933 --> 00:14:16,333
Who's causing trouble
here all the time?

339
00:14:16,333 --> 00:14:18,667
Come on, enough.

340
00:14:18,667 --> 00:14:20,800
Let's just do what
Gloria's asking us to do.

341
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:22,233
Come on!
Let's move these!

342
00:14:22,233 --> 00:14:24,033
- All right.
- Here.

343
00:14:25,167 --> 00:14:26,500
I see you're back.

344
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:27,600
[ROSA GULPS]

345
00:14:29,433 --> 00:14:32,100
You're back, General!

346
00:14:32,100 --> 00:14:33,500
Good... Good morning.

347
00:14:35,233 --> 00:14:37,100
So you know I'm a general.

348
00:14:37,100 --> 00:14:40,000
Yet you still have the nerve
to put up this act.

349
00:14:42,500 --> 00:14:43,633
Because...

350
00:14:44,733 --> 00:14:48,100
Madam Rosa is not brave,
General.

351
00:14:48,100 --> 00:14:51,000
Madam Rosa is... gifted.

352
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:52,467
Gifted!

353
00:14:52,467 --> 00:14:58,667
[COMICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

354
00:14:58,667 --> 00:15:01,000
Perhaps my wife
needs you right now.

355
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,067
She needs a...

356
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:04,633
shoulder to cry on,

357
00:15:04,633 --> 00:15:09,300
someone who'll tell her
everything will be okay.

358
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:13,467
[MUSIC TURNS PENSIVE]

359
00:15:13,467 --> 00:15:16,333
But I hope you don't
take advantage of Isobel.

360
00:15:16,933 --> 00:15:17,967
[ISOBEL CLEARS THROAT]

361
00:15:19,267 --> 00:15:21,300
Come with me.

362
00:15:21,300 --> 00:15:22,733
Oh, Ricardo!

363
00:15:22,733 --> 00:15:24,200
- It's good that you're there.
- [ROSA SIGHS IN RELIEF]

364
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:26,400
- Isobel, you're back!
- Oh.

365
00:15:26,400 --> 00:15:29,433
Do you want Madam Rosa
to read your fortune?

366
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:31,833
No, thank you.

367
00:15:31,833 --> 00:15:33,667
I just wanted to
make it clear to her that,

368
00:15:33,667 --> 00:15:37,767
even though
we let her come here freely,

369
00:15:38,733 --> 00:15:41,700
it doesn't mean she can do
whatever she wants.

370
00:15:41,700 --> 00:15:43,767
Oh my goodness, Ricardo.

371
00:15:43,767 --> 00:15:45,700
Max takes after you.

372
00:15:45,700 --> 00:15:47,667
You are both so skeptical.

373
00:15:48,900 --> 00:15:49,867
I know.

374
00:15:52,467 --> 00:15:53,767
So, are we clear?

375
00:15:53,767 --> 00:15:57,167
[STAMMERING]
Crystal clear, General.

376
00:16:03,267 --> 00:16:06,533
- [EXHALES HEAVILY]
- Don't mind my husband.

377
00:16:06,533 --> 00:16:09,233
By the way,
please accept this.

378
00:16:09,267 --> 00:16:11,933
- Oh, Isobel, you don't have to.
- Please, Madam Rosa.

379
00:16:11,933 --> 00:16:13,700
- No, no, no.
- Please take it.

380
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:16,133
Your company
is more than enough.

381
00:16:16,133 --> 00:16:17,600
- No...
- It's okay, Isobel.

382
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:20,067
I want to help you.
Take it.

383
00:16:20,067 --> 00:16:21,267
Take it.

384
00:16:23,333 --> 00:16:25,400
- Take it?
- Yes.

385
00:16:25,400 --> 00:16:27,033
Thank you.

386
00:16:28,100 --> 00:16:35,100
Isobel, you're more
than a friend to me.

387
00:16:35,100 --> 00:16:37,800
You're like a sister.

388
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:42,667
Just promise, Madam, that
if you feel Samantha's presence,

389
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:44,333
please let me know.

390
00:16:44,333 --> 00:16:47,300
I am so desperate.

391
00:16:47,300 --> 00:16:50,000
I want to talk to her.
Please.

392
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,967
I want to hear from her.

393
00:16:51,967 --> 00:16:54,667
Yes, Isobel.
Uh...

394
00:16:54,667 --> 00:16:58,367
Once Madam Rosa
gets a good night's sleep,

395
00:16:58,367 --> 00:17:02,400
which she's sure to get now,

396
00:17:03,067 --> 00:17:05,433
she will be able to
speak to Samantha.

397
00:17:05,433 --> 00:17:07,900
I miss my baby.

398
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:10,233
I miss my youngest daughter.

399
00:17:10,233 --> 00:17:12,467
- I miss her so much.
- [MADAM ROSA COUNTING]

400
00:17:12,467 --> 00:17:17,367
- 10, 11... 15... 17...
- [ISOBEL SOBS SOFTLY]

401
00:17:18,800 --> 00:17:21,133
- [GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]

402
00:17:21,133 --> 00:17:22,267
[SAM] How many?

403
00:17:23,300 --> 00:17:24,767
This doesn't go there.

404
00:17:24,767 --> 00:17:27,033
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

405
00:17:27,033 --> 00:17:28,500
- Where do I put it?
- [BOTTLES CLINKING]

406
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:32,267
- Hurry up so we can go home.
- What about this?

407
00:17:32,267 --> 00:17:34,333
- That's garbage.
- [CONTAINERS CLINKING]

408
00:17:34,333 --> 00:17:36,600
- They're empty.
- Throw 'em away.

409
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:38,000
Put those away.

410
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,000
Gloria, I got these
from our house.

411
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:41,867
- That's a lot.
- This is perfect.

412
00:17:41,867 --> 00:17:43,100
I'll put it here.

413
00:17:43,100 --> 00:17:46,433
Hey, Gloria, what are you
planning to do with these?

414
00:17:46,433 --> 00:17:48,167
After we clean them up,

415
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:49,700
we can make money
from them.

416
00:17:49,700 --> 00:17:51,133
Some can be turned into pots,

417
00:17:51,133 --> 00:17:53,333
while others can be
made into water sprinklers

418
00:17:53,333 --> 00:17:55,800
We can turn the others
into Christmas decor.

419
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:59,067
Great idea.
We could use the money.

420
00:17:59,067 --> 00:18:00,400
Mm-hmm.

421
00:18:00,400 --> 00:18:03,933
That's really the purpose
of all of this.

422
00:18:03,933 --> 00:18:07,467
We can help people
quit their vices

423
00:18:07,467 --> 00:18:10,233
and have them
do something useful instead.

424
00:18:10,233 --> 00:18:12,100
- Yes.
- There.

425
00:18:12,100 --> 00:18:14,233
[RUDY] Help them out, Dante.

426
00:18:14,233 --> 00:18:16,867
What do you want me to do?
Oh...

427
00:18:16,867 --> 00:18:18,100
I got it!

428
00:18:18,100 --> 00:18:23,167
What if we just burn it
so we can finish quickly?

429
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:25,433
- Huh?
- You didn't think of that.

430
00:18:25,433 --> 00:18:27,300
You're really incompetent.

431
00:18:27,300 --> 00:18:30,167
- Gloria will get mad.
- So what if she gets mad?

432
00:18:30,167 --> 00:18:32,200
Who'd you rather piss off,
me or her?

433
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:34,167
- [TOLITS] That's enough.
- [DABOY] I was just concerned.

434
00:18:34,167 --> 00:18:37,100
- You wimp.
- [TOLITS] Tekla has a point.

435
00:18:37,100 --> 00:18:40,533
Plus, I think Gloria will be
happy if we finish quickly.

436
00:18:40,533 --> 00:18:41,833
We'd be the first group
to finish!

437
00:18:41,833 --> 00:18:43,267
- That's right!
- That'll make her happy.

438
00:18:43,267 --> 00:18:45,133
I don't care if
it'll make her happy or not.

439
00:18:45,133 --> 00:18:47,433
I just want to
get this over with.

440
00:18:47,433 --> 00:18:48,400
Come on, let's go.

441
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:50,367
- Are you sure about this?
- Go ahead.

442
00:18:50,367 --> 00:18:51,967
Hey, wait a minute.

443
00:18:51,967 --> 00:18:53,400
Are you sure about that?

444
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:55,733
What if we burn the
whole place down?

445
00:18:55,767 --> 00:18:58,800
Wait a minute.
You're being paranoid.

446
00:18:58,800 --> 00:19:00,500
- Yeah.
- Come on!

447
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:02,300
- Just do it.
- I want to go home.

448
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:05,000
- Do it, man.
- Come on.

449
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:07,300
- There you go.
- [MATCHSTICK CLICKS]

450
00:19:07,300 --> 00:19:09,567
- There's the fire.
- [FIRE ERUPTS]

451
00:19:09,567 --> 00:19:11,367
- The fire's small.
- Let's add some more.

452
00:19:11,367 --> 00:19:13,333
- Let's go eat!
- See?

453
00:19:13,333 --> 00:19:14,900
[CHEERING, LAUGHING]

454
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:17,133
[FIRE ERUPTS, EXPLODES]

455
00:19:17,133 --> 00:19:19,133
[GROANING]

456
00:19:19,133 --> 00:19:21,433
- What happened?
- Are you okay?

457
00:19:21,433 --> 00:19:23,333
[GROANING IN PAIN]

458
00:19:23,333 --> 00:19:24,767
Are you okay?

459
00:19:24,767 --> 00:19:25,267
[COUGHING]

460
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:28,833
- Ouch!
- [COUGHS]

461
00:19:30,033 --> 00:19:32,833
What happened?
Why did this explode?!

462
00:19:34,267 --> 00:19:35,767
Daboy, are you alright?

463
00:19:37,767 --> 00:19:39,467
[BONG] Oh, it hurts!

464
00:19:39,467 --> 00:19:41,200
It hurts so much!

465
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:42,967
Who did that?! Who?!

466
00:19:44,800 --> 00:19:47,233
[BINOY] Who are you?
Who are you?!

467
00:19:47,867 --> 00:19:48,833
[TOLITS] Look at him.

468
00:19:48,833 --> 00:19:51,400
He's faking amnesia
so he won't get blamed.

469
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:52,333
[DABOY] Wait.

470
00:19:53,033 --> 00:19:54,200
I got burned too.

471
00:19:54,567 --> 00:19:55,467
[BONG] Yes.

472
00:19:55,467 --> 00:19:57,100
But you've always
looked like that.

473
00:19:58,133 --> 00:20:00,567
[BINOY] Who am I?!
What's my name?!

474
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:02,633
What happened?!

475
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,500
[IPE] It was Binoy.

476
00:20:04,500 --> 00:20:07,767
He lit up all the trash,
which is why it exploded.

477
00:20:07,767 --> 00:20:09,667
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

478
00:20:09,667 --> 00:20:12,267
Whose bright idea
was this anyway?

479
00:20:12,267 --> 00:20:13,267
Hmm?

480
00:20:15,233 --> 00:20:16,867
[SAM] C'mon, guys.

481
00:20:16,867 --> 00:20:18,967
Binoy,

482
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:22,000
burning trash has been
illegal for a long time.

483
00:20:22,400 --> 00:20:25,233
Aside from being dangerous,
it also pollutes the air

484
00:20:25,233 --> 00:20:27,667
That's why we're
cleaning up properly here.

485
00:20:27,667 --> 00:20:29,233
so we don't cause
trouble for others.

486
00:20:29,233 --> 00:20:31,100
Please I'm scared!

487
00:20:32,267 --> 00:20:33,800
- Who's Binoy?
- [DABOY] Oh no.

488
00:20:34,167 --> 00:20:35,733
All his memories are gone!

489
00:20:35,767 --> 00:20:38,433
[BONG] Maybe we need
to punch his face so--

490
00:20:38,433 --> 00:20:40,233
- Go ahead.
- You're right.

491
00:20:41,267 --> 00:20:42,600
Bong?! Tolits?!

492
00:20:44,067 --> 00:20:45,267
- Bitoy?
- Tolits?!

493
00:20:46,100 --> 00:20:46,967
Tolits!

494
00:20:46,967 --> 00:20:48,467
- Tolits!
- His memories are back.

495
00:20:48,467 --> 00:20:49,267
See?

496
00:20:49,267 --> 00:20:51,000
I remember now!

497
00:20:51,567 --> 00:20:52,633
Are you okay now?

498
00:20:53,367 --> 00:20:54,900
[TOLITS] It's me! I'm back!

499
00:20:54,900 --> 00:20:56,967
Don't start any fires
next time, okay?

500
00:20:57,933 --> 00:20:59,600
Let's get back to work!

501
00:20:59,600 --> 00:21:01,767
Don't start any fire, okay?

502
00:21:01,767 --> 00:21:03,133
- Let's get back to work! Now!
- Are you okay?

503
